From 130ef34f1a538496d9d3bbde8663f6dd03476775 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Vicory <dvicory@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 22:28:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gondolin): add a broker-backed terminal environment

Integrate Gondolin over HTTP/1.1 on the profile's mode-restricted Unix socket.
Hermes supplies canonical environment keys, commands, typed file operations,
and a board-qualified task-run envelope; the broker retains authority over VM
generation, policy, filesystem mediation, and resource ceilings.

Stream NDJSON output into existing process handles without duplicating final
output, preserve file bytes outside terminal text, and expose only capabilities
the backend implements. Backend-keyed tool schemas hide unsupported process
stdin while terminal registration remains stable during broker outages.

Treat cancellation as an authority transition rather than a local socket close:
close the exact captured environment generation, publish exit 130 only after a
closed acknowledgement, surface failed acknowledgements, and re-ensure before
later commands. Reject execution keys that differ from the trusted pre-spawn
binding so control and execution routes address the same workspace.
